# MCP identity (GDH admin vs mailbox)

This workstation has two Entra identities. They must stay split.

- Mailbox / Teams / Windows: the non-admin work account. Leave it signed in.
- Azure and Azure DevOps in Cursor: `jakobijn.strobbe.admin@denhaag.nl` via Azure PowerShell device-code login.

## Hard rules

- `C:\Users\BVJSTRO\.cursor\mcp.json` must keep both servers on `AZURE_TOKEN_CREDENTIALS=AzurePowerShellCredential`.
- Azure DevOps MCP must use `--authentication env` and `--tenant 8c653938-6726-49c5-bca7-8e44a4bf2029`.
- Never set Azure DevOps MCP to `--authentication interactive`.
- Never set `AZURE_MCP_ONLY_USE_BROKER_CREDENTIAL=true`.
- Never call `mcp_auth` on Azure or Azure DevOps MCP. That opens Windows Web Account Manager and selects the mailbox account.
- Do not add the admin UPN as a Windows work or school account.

If MCP shows the wrong projects or cannot write to PMO Cloud Platforms, run `C:\Users\BVJSTRO\.cursor\Connect-GdhAdminAz.ps1` in a normal PowerShell window, then reload Cursor. Do not re-authenticate MCP through a WAM picker.
